---
title: Turkey Larb Lettuce Wraps
course: main
cuisine: thai
servings: 4
time_active: 20
time_total: 25
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight, quick]
description: Thai-style ground turkey with lime, fish sauce, ginger, and fresh herbs, spooned into lettuce cups.
---

Toast @?jasmine rice{2%tbsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium, shaking the pan, until deep golden, ~{5%minutes}. Grind it coarsely in a spice grinder or mortar and set aside.

Whisk together @fish sauce{3%tbsp}, the juice of @limes{3}, @honey{2%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}.

Heat @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in the skillet over medium-high. Add @ground turkey{1%lb} and cook, breaking it into small crumbles, until no longer pink, ~{5-6%minutes}.

Add @shallots{2}(thinly sliced), @ginger{1%tbsp}(grated), and @garlic{2%clove}(minced). Cook until the shallots soften, ~{2%minutes}. Take the pan off the heat.

Pour in the dressing and toss. Let it cool a couple of minutes, then fold in @cilantro{1/2%bunch}(chopped), @mint{1/2%cup}(leaves, torn), @scallions{3}(thinly sliced), and the toasted rice powder. Taste: it should be sour, salty, and a little spicy. Add more lime or fish sauce to get there.

Spoon into leaves of @butter lettuce{2%head}(or little gem) and serve with steamed @?jasmine rice{}.

> For leftovers, store the turkey apart from the lettuce and herbs. It's good cold or warm over rice for lunch. Keeps 3 days.
